{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decision on 108e7b79 (G1 base possession and initial import verification), following checker 637088c4 and c9a2c676.\n\n1. Trust basis for incremental send: host ref connectivity under compare-and-swap. A destination provider may declare the capability \"retains-ref-closure@1\": the host stores no ref whose closure it does not hold (Git receive-pack connectivity). Incremental send may then omit base objects only when (a) the base is the destination ref's exact current value, (b) the send is a CAS whose old value is that base, and (c) repository identity, object format and namespace match the certificate in point 2. The CAS outcome is the proof: if the ref moved, the send fails and nothing is inherited. No lease or generation counter beyond the CAS old value is needed.\n2. Initial import verification: one bounded, resumable complete local closure verification per imported head. Its result is a certificate bound to repository identity, object format, base commit and tree, and validation policy version (v1). Invalidate it on any change of these, or when the destination ref is not the certified commit at send.\n3. Providers that do not declare retains-ref-closure@1 (all current ones until reviewed) keep the current full-closure send. G1 reports \"unavailable: provider has no reviewed retention capability\", not a silent fallback. Import must show uncompleted verification as such.\n4. Keep own-answer plus readback, unknown lost reply, no hidden retry. G0b partial retrieval continues independently and switches no caller.\n\nChecker reviews the capability declaration and the certificate shape in the first G1 Source. No deploy."}